meta {
  name: Lead Pull - Latest Run
  type: http
  seq: 22
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/meta/lead-pull/runs/latest?tenant_id={{tenantId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

docs {
  The tenant's current pull run, or data: null when it has none.

  Returns { run_id, status } — what /dashboard/lead-pull reopens on load. A new
  Pull deletes the tenant's previous run, so there is at most one. Before this
  route existed the run id lived only in the page's React state: leaving the
  page mid-pull lost it, and a completed-but-unapplied run could not be reopened
  at all.

  Regression checks:
    * tenant with no run ever                 -> 200, data: null (not 404)
    * after POST /runs                        -> that run_id, status queued/running
    * after a second POST /runs               -> the NEW run_id only
    * as tenant A, while tenant B has a run   -> data: null (the policy hides B's)
    * a bogus tenant_id                       -> 404 "Tenant not found"
    * caller below super_admin                -> 403
    * the gateway does NOT route "latest" into GET /runs/:runId (would 422 on a
      non-uuid run id)
}
